<!-- NFS FAQ Schema (mu-plugin) -->
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nestfumigationservices.com/sofa-cleaning-karachi/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does sofa cleaning cost in Karachi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A 3-seater fabric clean runs PKR 4,500–6,000 (cotton/polyester) or 5,500–7,500 (velvet/microfibre); full-grain leather is PKR 2,500–4,500 per seat with conditioning included. Heavy soiling adds 25%. We confirm a firm band on inspection — light vs heavy is only obvious once our SPMA-certified technician sees the sofa in your light."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between dry cleaning and wet sofa cleaning?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Wet cleaning (hot-water extraction at 70–80°C with anionic SLS surfactant) flushes deep soil from synthetics and microfibre. Dry/low-moisture encapsulation brushes a neutral-pH crystallising polymer into cotton, linen and velvet, then vacuums the dry residue. We pick by fabric — wet on synthetics, dry on naturals — never one method for every sofa."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does sofa cleaning take to dry?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Hot-water extraction on synthetic or microfibre sofas is touch-dry in 3–5 hours and foam-dry in 18–24. Velvet and other low-moisture cleans dry in 2–3 hours. Leather is dry immediately. We bring high-velocity air movers to every extraction job; running your AC at 22–24°C dehumidifies the room and accelerates drying measurably."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is sofa cleaning chemistry safe for leather?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — provided pH is right. We clean leather only with neutral pH 6.5–7.5 soap, distilled-water rinse, and a conditioning cream buffed in. Alkaline cleaners strip the natural oils and crack the hide within weeks. Conditioning is included in our leather pricing because uncleaned leather in dry-AC drawing rooms cracks within a year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I clean my sofa myself with home methods?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Light surface wipes are fine, but DIY usually fails on Karachi sofas. Home cleaners are unbuffered against the city's 250–350 ppm CaCO3 hard water, leaving white salt rings. Over-wetting wicks brown tide-marks up cotton and linen, and home solvents bleed dye on velvet. Professional EDTA-chelated chemistry plus moisture-controlled extraction avoids those failures."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should I get professional sofa cleaning?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Adult-only Karachi homes: every 9–12 months. Homes with young children: every 4–6 months. Homes with pets: every 3–4 months — dander and body oil accumulate faster than human soil. Weekly vacuuming with an upholstery attachment between cleans extends fabric life. If the seat shows a darker shadow than the back, you have waited too long."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you clean velvet, silk, or microfibre sofas?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — each gets distinct chemistry. Velvet: low-moisture shampoo brushed along the pile, then pile-lift. Silk-blend: cool non-ionic solvent at pH ≤7.5, no enzymes (they attack the protein fibre). Microfibre: hot-water extraction with mildly alkaline pre-treat and encapsulation rinse. We test every fabric in a hidden seam before touching a visible panel."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will sofa cleaning remove deep stains like ink or oil?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often, yes. Ballpoint and oil stains lift with d-limonene citrus solvent; chai and tannin marks respond to an acid rinse at pH 3–4 (citric acid); blood and protein stains need a cold protease enzymatic dwell — hot water sets them. Set-in pet urine, bleach marks and sun-faded panels are permanent. We tell you honestly before starting."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the cleaning chemistry safe for children and pets?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Our standard range is low-residue; for infants and pets we switch to a plant-derived kit (coconut-derived surfactants, citric acid, no fragrance, no optical brighteners). We skip BAC 0.06% and 200 ppm quat sanitisation on wool and silk. Tell us at booking. Keep kids and pets out of the room during cleaning and the first hour after."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you bundle sofa cleaning with carpet or full-house deep cleaning?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — bundles get a discount. Two or more sofas, or sofa plus carpet or mattress, is standard. NFS is ISO 9001:2015 certified and a member of SPMA, PPMA and KCCI; we run the same three-stage discipline across every service. WhatsApp seat count and fabric to +92-311-1101810 and we will quote a combined band within one working day."}}]}</script>

